        "text": "I'll analyze the California statute carefully. Key observation: Under §86113, the LOBBYIST prepares a periodic report and provides it to the lobbyist employer/lobbying firm, who then files it with the Secretary of State as part of their report (§86114(a)(4), §86116(e)). So the lobbyist's report is incorporated into the firm/employer's filing — the lobbyist is NOT the named filer of a separate spending report with the state. The filers under §86114 and §86116 are the lobbying firm and lobbyist employer.\n\nFor rows that explicitly require the LOBBYIST to be the named filer of a separate spending report, the answer is FALSE per the framing instructions.",
